The rain has stopped for now, so it is very crowded in the market.
I stop near a small shop of old things.
A lot of stuff is kept on the table here.
Five months ago, I did not use to stop at such shops.
But now I like these very much.
An elderly man is sitting at the shop.
I look at a small brass bell kept nearby.
"Uncle, how much is this bell for?" I ask.
He looks at me and smiles.
"Child, this is for two hundred rupees," he says.
Then I see a wooden box kept on the top shelf.
"And that box?" I ask.
"Is that also old?"
He turns back and looks.
"Yes, that is very old," he tells me.
"That box is for five hundred rupees."
I look at both things carefully.
"Thank you Uncle, these are very beautiful," I say.
But I do not buy anything today.
I just smile and walk on.
